www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512475/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Michigan expected to start Bryce Underwood vs. UCLA","description":"Michigan returned to QB Bryce Underwood vs. No. 4 UCLA after Tommy Carr had started the past four games, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-21T19:00:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50549879/sources-michigan-expected-start-bryce-underwood-vs-ucla","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Texas A&M expected to bench Marcel Reed, start Brady Hart","description":"Texas A&M is expected to make a change at quarterback, going with sophomore Brady Hart over Marcel Reed against Oklahoma, sources confirmed to ESPN.","published":"2026-11-21T15:29:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50549670/sources-texas-expected-bench-marcel-reed-vs-sooners","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oregon RB Dierre Hill Jr. limps off with injury in win vs. Michigan State","description":"Oregon running back Dierre Hill Jr. limped off the field with an injury in the first quarter against Michigan State.","published":"2026-11-21T19:12:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50545816/oregon-running-back-dierre-hill-exits-vs-michigan-state-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Revised Protect College Sports Act allows conferences to expand up to 22 schools","description":"Federal lawmakers published a revised version of the Protect College Sports Act on Friday as the U.S. House of Representatives prepares to push for a vote during the first week of December. President Donald Trump also voiced his support for the bill.","published":"2026-11-21T02:51:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50545220/protect-college-sports-act-revised-donald-trump-voices-support","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Dan Murphy","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"College football games this weekend: Top 25 schedule","description":"Here's what to know about the college football slate for the Top 25 this weekend.","published":"2026-11-20T21:19:52.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50542897/college-football-games-top-25-schedule-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4702828/aj-holmes-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A._J._Holmes_Jr."},"pick":{"pick":41,"round":2,"team":"NO","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"A. J. Holmes Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A._J._Holmes_Jr.","description":"American football player (born 2003)","touched":"2026-11-17T20:12:17Z","intro":"Anthony \"A. J.\" Holmes Jr. (born November 7, 2003) is an American college football defensive tackle for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. He previously played for the Houston Cougars.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Holmes Jr. attended Westfield High School in Houston, Texas. As a senior season, he was named the District 14-6A MVP. Coming out of high school, Holmes Jr. committed to play college football for the Houston Cougars over other offers from schools such as TCU, Kansas State, Washington State, SMU, and Virginia."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"HOUSTON\nDuring his freshman season in 2022, Holmes Jr. notched six tackles with half a tackle being for a loss. In the 2023 season, he appeared in 12 games with three starts, where he totaled 21 tackles with four and a half going for a loss, and two and a half sacks. During the 2024 season, Holmes Jr. tallied 40 tackles with eight and a half being for a loss, and two sacks. After the season, he entered his name into the NCAA transfer portal.\n\nTEXAS TECH\nHolmes Jr. transferred to play for the Texas Tech Red Raiders. In week 2 of the 2025 season, he notched four tackles with two being for a loss, a sack, a pass deflection, and a fumble recovery in a blowout win over Kent State. In week 6, Holmes Jr. recorded two sacks in a win versus Kansas. In week 7, he recorded a sack against Arizona State. For his performance during the 2025 season, Holmes Jr. was named a first-team All-American by Pro Football Focus."}]}}